[size=6][b]Concentration Redux[/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Dual-Stance Spellcasting Architecture for Baldur's Gate 3[/i][/size]

[line]

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
In D&D 5e and vanilla Baldur's Gate 3, nearly every iconic spell competes for a single, restrictive concentration slot. Casting a staple buff like [i]Bless[/i] or [i]Shield of Faith[/i] locks your caster out of using combat spells like [i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Call Lightning[/i], or [i]Hold Person[/i]. Worse, buffs vanish from a single 1-damage surface tick or an off-screen archer, and 10-turn timers expire while looting chests or reading dialogue.

[b]Concentration Redux[/b] redesigns spellcaster focus into two distinct, congruent cognitive layers:
[list]
[*][b]Focus (Buff Layer):[/b] Indefinite, damage-unbreakable utility and defensive wards ([i]Bless[/i], [i]Shield of Faith[/i], [i]Haste[/i], [i]Heroism[/i]).
[*][b]Concentration (Conduit Layer):[/b] High-intensity, stance-based combat conduits ([i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Fog Cloud[/i], [i]Moonbeam[/i]).
[*][b]The Overclock:[/b] Maintain both simultaneously! Pushes mental bandwidth to the limit with independent saving throws.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.[/b] Download the mod archive from the [b]Files[/b] tab.
[*][b]2.[/b] Import and install via [b]Vortex[/b] or [b]Baldur's Gate 3 Mod Manager (BG3MM)[/b].
[*][b]3.[/b] Ensure [b]Concentration Redux[/b] is enabled in your active load order and export.
[*][b]4.[/b] Launch the game—safe to install mid-playthrough!
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Main features[/b][/size]

[size=4][color=#ffd700][b]1. Three Tactical Stances[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Pure Support (Solo Focus):[/b] Only Focus is active. [b]100% Unbreakable by Damage.[/b] No Constitution saves against damage ticks or surfaces. Indefinite duration until Long Rest or manual dismissal.
[*][b]Dedicated Juggernaut (Solo Concentration):[/b] Only a combat conduit is active. Uses the native engine concentration slot with standard Con saves (benefits from War Caster). Whitelisted tactical actions ([i]Dash[/i], [i]Disengage[/i], [i]Shove[/i], [i]Throw[/i]). Weapon attacks allowed for martial domains ([i]War[/i] & [i]Tempest[/i]).
[*][b]The Overclock (Both Active Simultaneously):[/b] Maintain both Focus and Concentration at the same time! When damaged, the native conduit rolls standard saves, while Focus independently rolls a Constitution saving throw [b]with Advantage[/b]! If the combat conduit drops, Focus gracefully continues undisturbed.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#87cefa][b]2. Spell Classifications[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Focus Spells (Indefinite Buffs):[/b]
[list]
[*]Wards & Protection: [i]Bless[/i], [i]Shield of Faith[/i], [i]Guidance[/i], [i]Heroism[/i], [i]Protection from Evil and Good[/i], [i]Barkskin[/i], [i]Stoneskin[/i], [i]Shield of Thralls[/i]
[*]Single-Target Marks: [i]Hunter's Mark[/i], [i]Hex[/i], [i]Bane[/i], [i]Bestow Curse[/i] (reapplication abilities are whitelisted and never break active conduits)
[*]Augmentations & Stealth: [i]Haste[/i], [i]Enlarge/Reduce[/i], [i]Fly[/i], [i]Blur[/i], [i]Invisibility[/i], [i]Pass Without Trace[/i], [i]Detect Thoughts[/i]
[/list]
[*][b]Concentration Spells (Combat Conduits):[/b]
[list]
[*]Auras & Beams: [i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Aura of Vitality[/i], [i]Crusader's Mantle[/i], [i]Call Lightning[/i], [i]Moonbeam[/i], [i]Witch Bolt[/i], [i]Heat Metal[/i], [i]Sunbeam[/i], [i]Telekinesis[/i]
[*]Hazard Anchors: [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Cloud of Daggers[/i], [i]Fog Cloud[/i], [i]Darkness[/i], [i]Silence[/i], [i]Spike Growth[/i], [i]Sleet Storm[/i], [i]Hunger of Hadar[/i], [i]Cloudkill[/i]
[*]Hard CC: [i]Hold Person[/i], [i]Hold Monster[/i], [i]Hypnotic Pattern[/i], [i]Banishment[/i], [i]Tasha's Hideous Laughter[/i], [i]Slow[/i], [i]Confusion[/i]
[/list]
[/list]
[quote][b]Class Spells vs. Bound Gear & Scrolls:[/b] Genuine class investments utilize the full Focus system. Spells granted by equipment (e.g. Whispering Promise, Darkfire Shortbow) and consumable scrolls follow standard vanilla rules (10-turn limit, standard damage saves) to prevent item abuse.[/quote]

[size=4][color=#da70d6][b]3. UI & Visual Clarity[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Congruent Portrait Badges:[/b] Side-by-side badges in the portrait buff tray (Radiant Sun for [b]Focus[/b], glowing Mind Conduit for [b]Concentration[/b]).
[*][b]Dismissing Focus:[/b] Free, 0-action [b]Dismiss Focus[/b] ability added to your hotbar.
[*][b]Dismissing Concentration:[/b] Uses BG3's [b]native 'X' button[/b] beneath the portrait HUD (or casting another conduit).
[/list]

[size=4][color=#98fb98][b]4. Tactical Synergies & Rules[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Spellcasting Snaps Conduits:[/b] Channeling an active combat conduit ([i]Spirit Guardians[/i], [i]Wall of Fire[/i], [i]Call Lightning[/i]) demands 100% of your spellcasting bandwidth:
[list]
[*]Hard-casting any standard spell ([i]Fireball[/i], [i]Guiding Bolt[/i], [i]Magic Missile[/i]) immediately snaps your active conduit. (Casting a Focus buff like [i]Bless[/i] or [i]Shield of Faith[/i] enters [b]The Overclock[/b]).
[*]Casting emergency reaction spells ([i]Shield[/i], [i]Counterspell[/i], [i]Hellish Rebuke[/i]) also snaps active conduits (clear in-game tooltip warnings provided).
[*][i]Non-spell reactions[/i] ([i]Warding Flare[/i], [i]Wrath of the Storm[/i], [i]Cutting Words[/i], [i]Uncanny Dodge[/i], [i]Deflect Missiles[/i]) expend no spell slots and are 100% safe to use!
[/list]
[*][b]Smites Shatter Conduits:[/b] Expending spell slots for magical strikes ([i]Divine Smite[/i], [i]Searing Smite[/i], [i]Thunderous Smite[/i], [i]Wrathful Smite[/i], [i]Blinding Smite[/i], etc.) requires a burst of spellcasting focus and [b]immediately shatters active combat conduits[/b] ([i]Spirit Guardians[/i]), displaying an overhead notice ([i]"Channel broken by Smite!"[/i]), while leaving passive Focus buffs ([i]Bless[/i], [i]Shield of Faith[/i]) completely undisturbed!
[*][b]Combat Channeling & Gish Archetypes:[/b] Making weapon attacks while maintaining an active combat conduit requires true mind-body magical discipline:
[list]
[*][b]War Domain & Tempest Domain Clerics[/b] (Level 1)
[*][b]Monks[/b] (Level 1+: core spiritual discipline and Ki control)
[*][b]Paladins & Rangers[/b] (Level 2+: when spellcasting unlocks; level 1 characters are mundane combatants)
[*][b]Bladesinger Wizards[/b] (Level 2+: the epitome of martial blade-magic and Bladesong)
[*][b]Circle of Spores Druids[/b] (Level 2+: frontline fungal melee brawlers / [i]Symbiotic Entity[/i])
[*][b]College of Swords & Valour Bards[/b] (Level 3+: blade flourishes and frontline battle skalds)
[*][b]Pact of the Blade Warlocks[/b] (Level 3+: bound pact weapon specialists & Hexblades)
[*][b]Eldritch Knight Fighters & Arcane Trickster Rogues[/b] (Level 3+: dedicated martial-arcane gishes)
[*][i]Mundane fighters (Champion/Battle Master), mundane rogues (Thief/Assassin), and Barbarians cannot attack without disrupting active Concentration.[/i]
[/list]
[*][b]Advantage Balance:[/b] Gish training allows weapon attacks while channeling, but [b]does not grant Advantage on concentration saving throws[/b] (Advantage remains strictly reserved for the [i]War Caster[/i] feat or advantage gear).
[*][b]War Caster Synergy:[/b] Grants Advantage to Channeling saves. Because Focus already rolls with Advantage during Overclock, [b]War Caster ensures BOTH independent saves have Advantage![/b] Casting [i]Shocking Grasp[/i] as an Opportunity Attack reaction via War Caster is fully permitted.
[*][b]Whitelisted Tactical Actions & Recasts:[/b] 
[list]
[*]Non-magical maneuvers ([i]Dash[/i], [i]Disengage[/i], [i]Shove[/i], [i]Throw[/i], [i]Dip[/i], [i]Dodge[/i], [i]Hide[/i]) never disrupt active conduits.
[*]Re-activating ongoing concentration conduits ([i]Call Lightning[/i], [i]Moonbeam[/i], [i]Sunbeam[/i], [i]Witch Bolt[/i], [i]Eyebite[/i], [i]Telekinesis[/i] recast/move) is fully whitelisted.
[*]Re-targeting marks ([i]Reapply Hunter's Mark[/i], [i]Reapply Hex[/i]) is free and preserves active conduits.
[/list]
[*][b]Loss of Control (5e Compliant):[/b] Hard incapacitation ([i]Stunned[/i], [i]Paralyzed[/i], [i]Petrified[/i], [i]Sleep[/i], [i]Unconscious[/i], [i]Downed[/i], [i]Dead[/i]) shatters Focus and all linked party buffs.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Baldur's Gate 3:[/b] Patch 7 or Patch 8+
[*][b]Script Extender:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]Baldur's Gate 3 Script Extender (BG3SE)[/url] (v32 or newer recommended)
[/list]

